      "topic": "The manual lookup table",
      "exam_objective": "Prepare the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Transform and load the data — Merge and append queries",
      "prompt": "A two-column merge is intended to match Orders(StoreID,BusinessDate) to Rates(StoreID,BusinessDate). An analyst picks the right-side columns in reverse order. Why is the preview empty despite matching pairs existing in the source?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "code": "Orders: StoreID=5 (Whole Number), BusinessDate=2026-10-01 (Date).\nRates: StoreID=5 (Whole Number), BusinessDate=2026-10-01 (Date).\nSelection order: Left [StoreID,BusinessDate]; Right [BusinessDate,StoreID].",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "The first right key is compared to StoreID and the second to BusinessDate; align selection order and data types."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Power Query matches all selected columns by their semantic names regardless of the clicking order, and automatically reorders the corresponding right-hand keys."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "The operation becomes Full Outer when composite keys are selected in different orders on the two sides."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Power Query only supports single-column joins; create a concatenated string key without checking collisions."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
