      "topic": "Pivot mechanics",
      "exam_objective": "Prepare the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Transform and load the data — Pivot, unpivot and transpose data",
      "prompt": "A wide spreadsheet contains Jan Actual, Feb Actual and later adds Mar Actual. The existing Power Query step unpivots only the first two columns. The new month is visible in the input but remains a separate output column. What change best preserves expected month expansion without accidentally unpivoting account identifiers?",
