        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Disable source control entirely to avoid all future merge conflicts while preserving shared branch history."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V80-038",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V80-038",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V09-PBIP-022",
      "topic": "Secret management in Power BI Project",
      "exam_objective": "Manage and secure Power BI",
      "exam_subobjective": "Secret management in Power BI Project",
      "prompt": "A Git repository tracks a PBIP model and report while deployment uses a service principal. A developer considers storing refresh passwords and app secrets directly in project text files so every contributor can publish. The repository is shared with a large team. Which governance design is appropriate?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_AUTHOR_DRAFT_NOT_CALIBRATED",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Commit secrets beside the model because Git history permanently hides removed passwords."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Keep deployment credentials in a managed secret store outside Git."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Embed the passwords in a DAX calculated table that is hidden from report fields."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Add a bookmark that masks credentials on the report page while retaining them in the repository."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V80-039",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V80-039",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V28-CONTEXT-021",
      "topic": "KEEPFILTERS intersection versus replacement",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "KEEPFILTERS intersection versus replacement",
      "prompt": "A Product[Color] slicer has {Red, Blue} selected. The same model contains 50 sales for Red, 20 for Blue, and 30 for Green. A measure uses `CALCULATE([Sales], KEEPFILTERS(Product[Color] = \"Blue\"))`. Assuming normal model relationships, what is the result?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_AUTHOR_DRAFT_NOT_CALIBRATED",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "The result is 70 because KEEPFILTERS ignores its Blue condition when Red is also selected."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "The result is 100 because KEEPFILTERS removes every existing Color filter."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "The result is 20 because KEEPFILTERS intersects the selected colors with Blue."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "The result is 50 because KEEPFILTERS always selects the first originally selected color."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V80-040",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V80-040",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V28-CONTEXT-022",
      "topic": "REMOVEFILTERS only one dimension",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "REMOVEFILTERS only one dimension",
      "prompt": "A sales page filters Year=2026 and Region=North. A matrix groups Category and displays Revenue. Finance wants each Category as a percentage of all categories **inside North in 2026**, not nationwide or across all years. What filter-modifier scope fits the denominator?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_AUTHOR_DRAFT_NOT_CALIBRATED",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Use `REMOVEFILTERS()` without arguments to eliminate all Year and Region filters as well."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Remove only Region and preserve Category, then label the ratio as share of North categories."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Compute each Category revenue divided by its own row revenue for every row."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Remove only Category filters, preserving Year and Region in the denominator."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V80-041",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V80-041",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V06-LIVE-010",
      "topic": "Build permission without workspace editing",
      "exam_objective": "Manage and secure Power BI",
      "exam_subobjective": "Build permission without workspace editing",
      "prompt": "A certified semantic model is maintained centrally. Report authors in another workspace need to build their own thin reports, but they must not change the original model and must remain subject to RLS as consumers. Which permission pattern merits evaluation?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_AUTHOR_DRAFT_NOT_CALIBRATED",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Grant appropriate Build permission on the model while withholding elevated workspace editing roles; validate RLS with actual identities."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Make every author a Contributor in the model workspace since elevated workspace roles enforce consumer RLS."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Give authors only screenshots of charts and claim those represent governed semantic-model reuse."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Disable model permissions completely and expect external report workspaces to access the model anonymously."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V80-042",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V80-042",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V06-LIVE-017",
      "topic": "Thin report after model field rename",
      "exam_objective": "Manage and secure Power BI",
      "exam_subobjective": "Thin report after model field rename",
      "prompt": "Five thin reports connect to the same centrally published model. The data team plans to rename a measure used by three reports, while keeping the numerical formula unchanged. One developer argues report breakage is impossible because the DAX expression is equivalent. What should the release manager check?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_AUTHOR_DRAFT_NOT_CALIBRATED",
      "options": [
        {
