        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Take one global latest date and drop every account not observed on that date."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Count the number of distinct observation dates."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-052",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-052",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-016",
      "topic": "Storage reduction",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Storage reduction",
      "prompt": "A 20-million-row fact carries unique GUID event IDs and high-cardinality free-text remarks that are never used in reports or relationships. Memory is the limiting factor. What should be tried first?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Enable bidirectional filtering on every relationship."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Convert every dimension to a single concatenated text field."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Create duplicate calculated text columns for each fact row."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Remove unused high-cardinality columns before loading and measure compression/performance."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-053",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-053",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-017",
      "topic": "Aggregations by grain",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Aggregations by grain",
      "prompt": "An order fact has 100 million transaction lines, while most visuals show revenue by month and product category. Finance needs exact line drillthrough only occasionally. What architecture can improve common-query performance?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Delete the detail table permanently to force every query to be fast."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Duplicate transaction lines so the report engine can parallelize more work."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Add a correctly grained aggregated fact or supported aggregation table for month/category and retain detail for drillthrough."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Sum a table of transaction IDs instead of revenue."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-054",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-054",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-018",
      "topic": "Mark date table validation",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Mark date table validation",
      "prompt": "An analyst creates a Date table with two rows for 2026-01-01 and a blank date value, then tries to mark it as the date table. What data-quality correction is needed?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Convert dates to customer names so all values become distinct strings."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Keep both duplicate dates and increase decimal precision."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Ensure the selected Date column has unique nonblank values spanning contiguous dates at day grain."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Set the Date-to-Fact relationship to Both."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-055",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-055",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-022",
      "topic": "Blank relationship member",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Blank relationship member",
      "prompt": "The Product dimension lacks ProductID 999, but Sales includes orders with ProductID 999. A chart grouped by Product[Category] shows a (Blank) member with revenue. What is the most likely root cause?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Sales has no records for category blank and all joins are guaranteed complete."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Referential integrity is violated: fact foreign keys have no matching dimension key; diagnose missing ProductID rows."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "The chart is sorted descending rather than ascending."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Using a sum measure automatically creates a new ProductID 999 row."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-056",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-056",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-024",
      "topic": "SELECTEDVALUE ambiguity",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "SELECTEDVALUE ambiguity",
      "prompt": "A measure displays a chosen CurrencyCode in a card. Two currencies are selected, so the label must say Multiple rather than choose an arbitrary currency. Which expression fits?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "SUM(Currency[Code])"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "MAX(Currency[Code]) with no fallback."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "COUNTROWS(Sales) formatted as a currency code."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "SELECTEDVALUE(Currency[Code], \"Multiple\")"
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-057",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-057",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-025",
      "topic": "ALLSELECTED visual percent",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "ALLSELECTED visual percent",
      "prompt": "In a matrix, users filter Year and Product Category through slicers. Within the visible product rows, they need each product’s share of the slicer-selected product total, not the global total. What DAX context pattern should be investigated?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Use a denominator evaluated over the visible selection, for example ALLSELECTED on the product-level axis, while validating the exact visual query context."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Divide each product revenue by itself."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Use REMOVEFILTERS() without columns in every denominator."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Use COUNTROWS(Product) as a revenue denominator."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-058",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-058",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-028",
      "topic": "Composite model cross-source relationships",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Composite model cross-source relationships",
      "prompt": "A composite model relates imported Customer dimension to a DirectQuery fact from another source group. A developer expects exactly the same join behavior as a regular Import relationship. What should be explicitly validated?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "All cross-source relationships behave as regular import relationships with blank virtual rows."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "DirectQuery automatically synchronizes the import dimension every visual query."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Set the page background to indicate DirectQuery."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Cross-source group relationships are limited and have different join/expansion behavior; verify unmatched keys and DAX function constraints."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-059",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-059",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-029",
      "topic": "Calculation group impact",
      "exam_objective": "Model the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Calculation group impact",
      "prompt": "A finance model contains 50 base measures and users require Current, Prior Year, and Year-over-Year transformations consistently. What is a defensible motivation for a calculation group?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Eliminate all relationships so every calculation group applies globally."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Centralize reusable calculation-item transformations rather than copying time-logic into many duplicated measures, while testing precedence and formatting."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Use calculation groups only to color chart headers and not modify expressions."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Store each fact row’s currency value in a calculation item."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-060",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-060",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V32-CALCTBL-033",
