      "topic": "Small multiples",
      "exam_objective": "Visualize and analyze the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Small multiples",
      "prompt": "Marketing wants twelve geographic regions each shown as a separate, consistently scaled mini line chart over time, for side-by-side trend comparison. Which visual configuration fits?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Use small multiples with Region as the splitting dimension, checking shared axes and labeling."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Replace daily time with numeric RegionID as the horizontal axis."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Plot all Region names as axis values in a single pie chart."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Use a dynamic security role per region to make one chart at a time."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-075",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-075",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V26-CAPSTONE-045",
      "topic": "KPI design",
      "exam_objective": "Visualize and analyze the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "KPI design",
      "prompt": "Executives need to see current revenue versus a target and the recent trend. A proposed pie chart has segments Actual and Target. What is the stronger design choice?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Use a map without geographic dimensions."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Use a KPI/card with target comparison and an appropriately scaled time-series trend."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Hide the target and report only current amount."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Use a pie where Actual and Target sum to a fictional total."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-076",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-076",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V26-CAPSTONE-046",
      "topic": "Top N with Other",
      "exam_objective": "Visualize and analyze the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Top N with Other",
      "prompt": "A category chart has 40 categories. The business wants the top five by profit and an explicit Other bar with the remaining categories’ total, not simply hidden categories. Which approach is correct?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Build a Top-N-plus-Other grouping or supporting measure that explicitly calculates the remaining total, then validate totals."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Remove all categories below average without reconciling the total."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Apply the built-in Top N filter and assume it creates an Other bar automatically."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Sort categories descending and rename the sixth category Other."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-077",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-077",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V26-CAPSTONE-050",
      "topic": "Page-level vs report-level filters",
      "exam_objective": "Visualize and analyze the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Page-level vs report-level filters",
      "prompt": "A Power BI report has four pages. A fiscal year filter must apply everywhere, while a Sales Channel filter should apply only to the Retail page. Where should the filters be assigned?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Both filters as filters on one Retail visual only."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Remove all filters and hope cross-highlighting enforces year globally."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Fiscal year at report level; Sales Channel at the Retail page level."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Fiscal year as a single visual filter and Sales Channel at report level."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-078",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-078",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V26-CAPSTONE-054",
      "topic": "Report accessibility tab order",
      "exam_objective": "Visualize and analyze the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Report accessibility tab order",
      "prompt": "A report includes decorative shapes, a date slicer, a navigation button and three charts. Keyboard users encounter decorative elements first and cannot reach key controls in logical order. What should the author do?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Use only color gradients to imply navigation order."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Configure meaningful visual/tab order and accessible names, excluding decorative elements from navigation where possible."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Remove all slicers so keyboard users have fewer stops."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Set every shape and visual to the same inaccessible title."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-079",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-079",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V26-CAPSTONE-055",
      "topic": "Dynamic format strings",
      "exam_objective": "Visualize and analyze the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Dynamic format strings",
      "prompt": "The same Revenue measure should display USD with currency symbols in one view and EUR with appropriate symbols in another, while remaining numeric for sorting and charts. Which solution is strongest?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Store revenue as a concatenation of currency name and numeric value in the fact."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Wrap the revenue measure in FORMAT and use that text as a chart numeric value."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Use a measure dynamic format string based on an appropriately modeled currency selection while keeping the underlying measure numeric."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Change the page title and assume all axes adopt the title’s currency."
        }
      ],
      "gradingEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "draftId": "draft-pl300-v88-PL300-SUPP-V81-080",
      "sourceId": "PL300-SUPP-V81-080",
      "legacy_id": "PBI-V26-CAPSTONE-056",
      "topic": "Cross-report drillthrough",
      "exam_objective": "Visualize and analyze the data",
      "exam_subobjective": "Cross-report drillthrough",
      "prompt": "Two reports exist in the same workspace and reference compatible fields. Users want an interactive drillthrough from a summary report into a detail report. What is required beyond placing a normal navigation button?",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "APPLIED_SCENARIO_PROVISIONAL",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Disable target report permissions for viewers."
